## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical incident response for streaming workloads with backpressure, not just static services.

## Key Concepts

- Lag metrics per partition and end-to-end tracing
- Alert thresholds for latency and lag
- Backpressure and scaling strategies (max_poll_records, HPA, rate limiting)
- Canary rollout and rollback with validation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-idempotent consumer outline
async function handle(msg) {
  if (await seen(msg.id)) return;
  await process(msg);
  await markSeen(msg.id);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the rollback plan under load?
- What are trade-offs of increasing partitions vs increasing consumer replicas?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to respond to production incidents with a concrete, beginner-friendly plan focusing on observable signals, containment, rollback, and validation under time pressure.

## Key Concepts
- Observability: latency p95, error rate, queue depth, redis/backlog metrics
- Containment: throttle concurrency, pause new work, revert patch safely
- Rollback & Validation: restore previous config, synthetic tests, end-to-end checks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple end-to-end validation stub
async function checkDelivery(queueClient, producer) {
  const msg = {id: 'test', payload: 'ping'};
  await producer.send(msg);
  const ok = await queueClient.awaitDeliveryAck(msg.id, 5000);
  return ok;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you automate the rollback trigger and rollback-on-fail thresholds?
- Which metrics would you add to distinguish transient spikes from persistent issues?

## Why Asked
Tests understanding of resilience patterns and operational excellence in distributed systems, which is essential for maintaining production reliability.

## Key Concepts
- Health monitoring and failure detection mechanisms
- Automated recovery and self-repair processes
- Circuit breakers and retry patterns
- Redundancy and failover strategies

## Code Example
```
class SelfHealingService {
  async monitor() {
    if (!await this.healthCheck()) {
      await this.restart();
      await this.circuitBreaker.reset();
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement circuit breakers?
- What monitoring tools would you use?
